            <ArticleTitle>Leiomyosarcoma of the infrarenal portion of the inferior vena cava in a cirrhotic patient with hepatitis C.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>222-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leiomyosarcoma of the inferior vena cava is a rare primary tumor. We present a case of a 65-year-old man with the history of cirrhosis and non-specific symptoms. The patient underwent computed tomography and magnetic resonance imaging that revealed a leiomyosarcoma of the infrarenal portion of inferior vena cava. Clinical and imaging features, as well as the surgical technique of resection are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
